SOUNDPROBE(1)

NAME
    soundprobe - exercise SmallOS sound devices

SYNOPSIS
    soundprobe

DESCRIPTION
    Plays short diagnostic samples through the SmallOS sound syscall surface.
    The probe checks the active PCM playback path and emits an AdLib/OPL2 tone
    when an AdLib-compatible device is present.  Its status output also reports
    active kernel-timed OPL music sequences and OPL effects.

NOTES
    For QEMU Wolf3D testing, expose AC97 for digitized effects and AdLib for
    FM sound effects and music:

        -audiodev sdl,id=audio0,in.voices=0,out.frequency=48000,out.buffer-length=50000
        -device AC97,audiodev=audio0
        -device adlib,audiodev=audio0

SEE ALSO
    wolf3d(1), smallos(7)
